# Project Overview

| Category | Details |
|---|---|
| **Domain** | Healthcare / Patient Experience |
| **BI Platform** | Microsoft Power BI |
| **Data Preparation** | Power Query |
| **Transformation Language** | M Query |
| **Analytical Language** | DAX |
| **Data Modeling** | Star Schema |
| **Analysis Period** | 2015–2023 |
| **Geographic Analysis** | National, Regional & State |
| **Primary Metric** | Top-Box Percentage |
| **AI Feature** | Power BI Q&A |
| **Advanced Visuals** | Gauge, Funnel, Shape Map, Decomposition Tree |

---

# Business Problem

HCAHPS data contains multiple patient-experience measures across reporting periods and geographic areas.

The objective of this project is to transform these related datasets into an interactive analytical solution that makes it easier to understand:

- Overall patient perception
- Willingness to recommend
- Performance of individual patient-experience dimensions
- State and regional differences
- Survey response-rate patterns
- Changes in Top-Box performance over time

The dashboard was designed around these analytical questions rather than simply presenting the underlying data.

---

# Business Objectives

The project focuses on:

- Evaluating overall patient-experience performance
- Monitoring Overall Hospital Rating
- Analyzing Willingness to Recommend
- Comparing patient-experience dimensions
- Tracking performance across reporting periods
- Identifying state-level variation
- Exploring regional differences
- Analyzing reported survey response rates
- Comparing Top-Box performance between 2015 and 2023
- Providing an interactive Power BI analytical solution

---

# Dataset

The project uses seven related HCAHPS tables.

| Table | Rows | Columns | Purpose |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| **Reports** | 9 | 4 | Reporting periods and start/end dates |
| **States** | 56 | 3 | State names, state codes, and regions |
| **Measures** | 10 | 3 | HCAHPS patient-experience measures |
| **Questions** | 19 | 6 | Survey questions mapped to measures |
| **National Results** | 90 | 8 | National Bottom-, Middle-, and Top-Box results |
| **State Results** | 4,580 | 9 | State-level results across measures and periods |
| **Responses** | 43,219 | 5 | Facility survey counts and reported response rates |

### Data Coverage

The dataset supports analysis across:

**National → Region → State → Reporting Period → Facility Response**

The seven source tables were maintained separately because they represent different analytical grains and serve different roles within the data model.

---

# HCAHPS Result Structure

The results contain three response categories:

| Category | Role |
|---|---|
| **Bottom-Box** | Lower response category |
| **Middle-Box** | Middle response category |
| **Top-Box** | Highest response category |

The dashboard primarily uses **Top-Box Percentage** when comparing patient-experience performance.

---

# Data Preparation

Data preparation was performed using **Power Query**.

## Key Transformations

| Transformation | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **Promote Headers** | Converted source rows into column headers |
| **Change Data Types** | Assigned appropriate data types to analytical fields |
| **Response Rate Transformation** | Created a numeric response-rate field while handling non-numeric values |
| **Percentage Validation** | Checked Bottom-, Middle-, and Top-Box percentage distributions |
| **Facility ID Preservation** | Kept Facility ID as Text to preserve alphanumeric identifiers and leading zeros |

### Response Rate Handling

The original response-rate field contained both numeric and non-numeric values.

A separate numeric field was created so that valid response-rate values could be analyzed while unavailable values remained blank.

### Data Validation

Percentage fields were checked during preparation to validate the response distributions before analysis.

![Power Query Transformations](screenshots/power_query.png)

---

# Data Model

The Power BI model follows a **Star Schema-oriented structure**.

## Dimension Tables

- Reports
- States
- Measures

## Fact Tables

- National Results
- State Results
- Responses

## Supporting Table

- Questions

### Relationship Design

The model uses:

- One-to-many relationships
- Active relationships
- Single-direction filtering
- No many-to-many relationships

![Power BI Data Model](screenshots/data_model.png)

---

# DAX & Analytical Layer

DAX was used to create the analytical measures required for KPI reporting, benchmarking, geographic analysis, and period comparisons.

## Key DAX Measures

| Measure | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **Overall Hospital Rating Top Box** | Latest national Overall Hospital Rating |
| **Willingness to Recommend Top Box** | Latest national Willingness to Recommend |
| **Historical Peak Overall Rating** | Highest recorded Overall Hospital Rating |
| **Average Response Rate** | Average of valid reported response rates |
| **State Top Box %** | State-level Top-Box analysis |
| **National Top Box %** | National measure comparison |
| **Top Box Change 2015 to 2023** | Change between 2015 and 2023 |

Additional calculated fields were used for reporting-period analysis and dashboard functionality.

![DAX Measures](screenshots/dax_measures.png)

---

# Key Performance Indicators

Two primary KPIs provide the high-level view of patient experience.

| KPI | 2023 Result | Purpose |
|---|---:|---|
| **Overall Hospital Rating Top Box** | **70%** | Overall patient perception indicator |
| **Willingness to Recommend Top Box** | **69%** | Patient recommendation indicator |

### Historical Benchmark

**Historical Peak Overall Hospital Rating: 73%**

The historical peak is used as a benchmark for comparing current Overall Hospital Rating performance.

---

# Dashboard Analysis

The dashboard combines KPI reporting, trend analysis, measure comparison, geographic analysis, and response-rate analysis.

## 1. Overall Rating vs Recommendation

### Business Question

**How have Overall Hospital Rating and Willingness to Recommend changed over time?**

A line chart compares both patient-perception indicators from 2015 through 2023.

---

## 2. Current vs Historical Peak

### Business Question

**How does the current Overall Hospital Rating compare with its historical peak?**

The gauge compares:

- **Current Overall Hospital Rating:** 70%
- **Historical Peak:** 73%

---

## 3. Patient Experience Dimensions

### Business Question

**Which patient-experience dimensions have stronger or weaker Top-Box performance in 2023?**

The funnel compares eight supporting measures.

| Measure | 2023 Top Box |
|---|---:|
| **Discharge Information** | **86%** |
| Communication with Doctors | 79% |
| Communication with Nurses | 79% |
| Cleanliness | 72% |
| Responsiveness | 65% |
| Quietness | 62% |
| Communication about Medicines | 61% |
| **Care Transition** | **51%** |

Overall Hospital Rating and Willingness to Recommend are treated as headline indicators and are not included in this supporting-measure comparison.

---

## 4. State Performance

### Business Question

**Which states show stronger or weaker Overall Hospital Rating performance in 2023?**

The Shape Map uses state-level Overall Hospital Rating Top-Box percentages to visualize geographic variation.

---

## 5. Survey Response Rate

### Business Question

**How does reported survey response rate vary across regions, states, and reporting periods?**

The Decomposition Tree allows hierarchical analysis through:

**Region → State → Reporting Period**

This provides a detailed view of reported survey response-rate variation.

---

